## Complexity
**Time Complexity:** 
O(N log N) The DFS traversal visits each node once, taking O(N) time. Storing nodes takes O(N) space. The sorting of N nodes takes O(N log N) time. The final loop to construct the answer takes O(N) time as each node is processed once. Therefore, the dominant factor is the sorting, resulting in O(N log N).

**Space Complexity:**
O(N) The `nodes` vector stores information for each of the N nodes, taking O(N) space. The recursion depth of DFS can be up to O(H) where H is the height of the tree, which in the worst case (a skewed tree) can be O(N). The `ans` vector can store up to N elements in total across its inner vectors. Thus, the total space complexity is O(N).
